{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-pointwise","title":"prop:hodge-star-pointwise","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":4132,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:hodge-star-pointwise","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hodge-scalar-identity]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-form-eq-of-basis]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-bilinear]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-comm-sum]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:inner-k-covectors]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:inner-k-covectors-posdef]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:inner-k-covectors-frame-independent]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:hodge-star-pointwise","line":7018,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Pointwise Hodge Star]\n\\label{prop:hodge-star-pointwise}\n\n\\uses{lem:hodge-scalar-identity, lem:top-form-eq-of-basis, lem:wedge-bilinear, lem:wedge-comm-sum, def:inner-k-covectors, lem:inner-k-covectors-posdef, prop:inner-k-covectors-frame-independent}\n\n\n\n\nFor a bijection $\\varepsilon:\\iota_a\\sqcup\\iota_b\\to\\iota'$ and $\\eta\\in\\Lambda^{\\iota_a}(V^*)$, set\n\\[\n{*}\\eta=\\frac1{l!}\\sum_{t:\\iota_b\\to\\iota'}B(\\eta,E^t)E^t.\n\\]\nThe map is linear, satisfies $\\omega\\wedge {*}\\eta=\\langle\\omega,\\eta\\rangle_eE^\\varepsilon$, is uniquely characterized by this identity, and is independent of orthonormal block data with the same reference volume form.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch Linearity is immediate. Compare the two top forms on $e\\circ\\varepsilon$ and use Lemma \\ref{lem:hodge-scalar-identity}. For uniqueness, the difference of two candidates wedges to zero with every form; the mirrored scalar identity and positive definiteness force it to vanish. Equal reference volumes and frame independence give the last assertion.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Pointwise Hodge Star] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f6467652d737461722d706f696e7477697365\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahodge-scalar-identity\">↗ lem:hodge-scalar-identity</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atop-form-eq-of-basis\">↗ lem:top-form-eq-of-basis</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awedge-bilinear\">↗ lem:wedge-bilinear</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awedge-comm-sum\">↗ lem:wedge-comm-sum</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainner-k-covectors\">↗ def:inner-k-covectors</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ainner-k-covectors-posdef\">↗ lem:inner-k-covectors-posdef</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ainner-k-covectors-frame-independent\">↗ prop:inner-k-covectors-frame-independent</a> <p></p>For a bijection <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varepsilon :\\iota _a\\sqcup \\iota _b\\to \\iota &#x27;$\">$\\varepsilon :\\iota _a\\sqcup \\iota _b\\to \\iota &#x27;$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\eta \\in \\Lambda ^{\\iota _a}(V^*)$\">$\\eta \\in \\Lambda ^{\\iota _a}(V^*)$</span>, set <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  {*}\\eta =\\frac1{l!}\\sum _{t:\\iota _b\\to \\iota &#x27;}B(\\eta ,E^t)E^t.  \\]\">\\[  {*}\\eta =\\frac1{l!}\\sum _{t:\\iota _b\\to \\iota &#x27;}B(\\eta ,E^t)E^t.  \\]</span> The map is linear, satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\omega \\wedge {*}\\eta =\\langle \\omega ,\\eta \\rangle _eE^\\varepsilon $\">$\\omega \\wedge {*}\\eta =\\langle \\omega ,\\eta \\rangle _eE^\\varepsilon $</span>, is uniquely characterized by this identity, and is independent of orthonormal block data with the same reference volume form.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Linearity is immediate. Compare the two top forms on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e\\circ \\varepsilon $\">$e\\circ \\varepsilon $</span> and use Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahodge-scalar-identity\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hodge-scalar-identity\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a686f6467652d7363616c61722d6964656e74697479\">3</a>. For uniqueness, the difference of two candidates wedges to zero with every form; the mirrored scalar identity and positive definiteness force it to vanish. Equal reference volumes and frame independence give the last assertion. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hodge-scalar-identity","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-degree-zero","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters